serial: sc16is7xx: return false instead of setting the removed rc

Stable commit 76a91352fbd6e ("serial: sc16is7xx: use guards for simple mutex
locks") converts sc16is7xx_port_irq() to guard(mutex) and removes the 'rc'
local and the out_port_irq label, returning directly. Downstream rpi-6.12.y
carries f9ac7286c1223 ("serial: sc16is7xx: Don't spin if no data received"),
that sets rc = false when no data was received. The stable commit merged
without conflict, leaving that assignment to an undeclared variable.

Return false directly, as the guard releases the lock on return.

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/sc16is7xx.c b/drivers/tty/serial/sc16is7xx.c
index e2eee7440d8c6..5abd8b945bc53 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/sc16is7xx.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/sc16is7xx.c
@@ -844,7 +844,7 @@ static bool sc16is7xx_port_irq(struct sc16is7xx_port *s, int portno)
 		if (rxlen)
 			sc16is7xx_handle_rx(port, rxlen, iir);
 		else
-			rc = false;
+			return false;
 		break;
 		/* CTSRTS interrupt comes only when CTS goes inactive */
 	case SC16IS7XX_IIR_CTSRTS_SRC:
